[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should be set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m ESLint + Prettier
  [38;5;246mAggressive linting and auto-formatting on the standard JS/Preact config. Near-zero cost to add now, annoying to [39m
  [38;5;246mretrofit across a grown codebase.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests (Vitest)
  [38;5;246mRunner, layout, and a first passing fixture. Strongly recommended here — the scheduler's threshold logic and the [39m
  [38;5;246mfired-set are pure functions and exactly what unit tests are for.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests (Playwright)
  [38;5;246mBrowser-level tests for the real flows: create a task, advance the clock, see the bell increment. Catches integration
[39m  [38;5;246mbugs unit tests miss; adds CI weight and a slower feedback loop.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Fuzz / property testing
  [38;5;246mProperty-based tests (fast-check) over the event log and scheduler — e.g. no duplicate notification for one crossing,
[39m  [38;5;246mregardless of event ordering. Useful given the fired-set's edge cases.[39m
